<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Transformers in Detail</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As stated, we focus on decoder-only transformers with softmax self-attention and no causal masking. We consider a multi-layer, multi-head transformer with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> transformer blocks and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads each. Each transformer block is defined as follows. For the block input <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the pre-activation</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z(X)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{H}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}A^{h}(X)V^{h}(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>H</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z(X)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{H}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}A^{h}(X)V^{h}(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with attention weights</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{h}(X)=\Softmax\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}Q^{h}(X)K^{h}(X)^{\top}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{h}(X)=\Softmax\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}Q^{h}(X)K^{h}(X)^{\top}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In particular, for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{z}_{a}(X)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{H}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{b=1}^{T}A^{h}_{ab}(X)V^{h}_{b}(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>H</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{z}_{a}(X)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{H}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{b=1}^{T}A^{h}_{ab}(X)V^{h}_{b}(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{h}(X)=XW^{h}_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{h}(X)=XW^{h}_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K^{h}(X)=XW^{h}_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K^{h}(X)=XW^{h}_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{h}(X)=XW^{h}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{h}(X)=XW^{h}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{h}_{Q},W^{h}_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{h}_{Q},W^{h}_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{h}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{h}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with each weight matrix entry sampled i.i.d. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W^{h}_{Q})_{i,j},(W^{h}_{K})_{i,j},(W^{h}_{V})_{i,j}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1/d_{\text{model}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W^{h}_{Q})_{i,j},(W^{h}_{K})_{i,j},(W^{h}_{V})_{i,j}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1/d_{\text{model}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Adding an MLP layer (or, more generally, some form of non-linearity), the output of the transformer block at the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>-th token is given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mlp(\bm{z}_{a})=\phi(\bm{z}_{a})W+\bm{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mlp(\bm{z}_{a})=\phi(\bm{z}_{a})W+\bm{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">for an activation function <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., ReLU), <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{b}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{b}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As input to the initial block, we will add an embedding from raw input dimension into the model’s internal representation space <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mathrm{emb}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>emb</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mathrm{emb}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This setup is intentionally simplified: we omit positional encoding, layer normalization, and the standard two-layer FFN/MLP (using instead a single pointwise nonlinearity followed by a linear map). We also omit the usual output projection <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, combining heads by averaging as in (<a href="#A1.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ A.1 Setup ‣ Appendix A Transformers in Detail ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Inference-time Complexity</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The inference-time complexity of a transformer is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> as we will now demonstrate. First, note that the number of FLOPs involved in multiplying matrices <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,k)\times(k,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,k)\times(k,n)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 2mkn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2mkn</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, calculating <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(X),K(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(X),K(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 2Td_{\text{model}}d_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2Td_{\text{model}}d_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and calculating <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 2Td_{\text{model}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2Td_{\text{model}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, calculating <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(X)K(X)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(X)K(X)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 2T^{2}d_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2T^{2}d_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Calculating <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Softmax" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Softmax</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Softmax</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(T^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(T^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, while multiplying by <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 2T^{2}d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 2T^{2}d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for the attention layer in a transformer block, we get</p>
<table id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\flops_{\mathrm{attn}}\approx H(4Td_{\text{model}}d_{k}+\\
2Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+2T^{2}d_{k}+\Theta(T^{2})+2T^{2}d_{\text{model}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>FLOPs</mi><mi>attn</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\flops_{\mathrm{attn}}\approx H(4Td_{\text{model}}d_{k}+\\
2Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+2T^{2}d_{k}+\Theta(T^{2})+2T^{2}d_{\text{model}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As for the MLP block, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\flops_{\mlp}\approx 2Td_{\text{model}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>FLOPs</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\flops_{\mlp}\approx 2Td_{\text{model}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. And together, we get</p>
<table id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\flops_{\mathrm{block}}=\\
O(H\left[Td_{\text{model}}d_{k}+Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+T^{2}(d_{k}+d_{\text{model}})\right])" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>FLOPs</mi><mi>block</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\flops_{\mathrm{block}}=\\
O(H\left[Td_{\text{model}}d_{k}+Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+T^{2}(d_{k}+d_{\text{model}})\right])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">For a typical choice <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k}=d_{\text{model}}/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k}=d_{\text{model}}/H</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\flops_{\mathrm{block}}=O\left(H\left[Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+T^{2}d_{\text{model}}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>FLOPs</mi><mi>block</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\flops_{\mathrm{block}}=O\left(H\left[Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+T^{2}d_{\text{model}}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">And for a transformer with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> blocks</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\flops_{\mathrm{trans}}=O\left(LH\left[Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+T^{2}d_{\text{model}}\right]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>FLOPs</mi><mi>trans</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\flops_{\mathrm{trans}}=O\left(LH\left[Td_{\text{model}}^{2}+T^{2}d_{\text{model}}\right]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Following our discussion in <a href="#S5" title="5 Tighter Bounds and Feature Learning ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, when <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}\propto\log(T)^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}\propto\log(T)^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have computational complexity scaling of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> times negligible logarithmic corrections.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Kernel Propagation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Kernel propagation through network layers was considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2018</a>)</cite> for deep FCNs. Their propagation rule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2018</a>, Eq. (4))</cite> applies, in our case, as we pass through the MLP layer</p>
<table id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mlp(\bm{z}_{a}(X_{1}))^{\top}\mlp(\bm{z}_{b}(X_{2}))]=\\
\sigma_{\bm{b}}^{2}+\sigma_{W}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\left(z_{a}(X_{1}),z_{b}(X_{2})\right)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,k)}\left[\phi\left(\bm{z}_{a}(X_{1})\right)\phi\left(\bm{z}_{b}(X_{2})\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝒃</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mlp(\bm{z}_{a}(X_{1}))^{\top}\mlp(\bm{z}_{b}(X_{2}))]=\\
\sigma_{\bm{b}}^{2}+\sigma_{W}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\left(z_{a}(X_{1}),z_{b}(X_{2})\right)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,k)}\left[\phi\left(\bm{z}_{a}(X_{1})\right)\phi\left(\bm{z}_{b}(X_{2})\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,k)</annotation></semantics></math> is the bi-variate Gaussian distribution with the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> covariance matrix <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> define via</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k_{aa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k_{aa}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Sigma_{aa}(X_{1},X_{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Sigma_{aa}(X_{1},X_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=k_{ba}=\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=k_{ba}=\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k_{bb}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k_{bb}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Sigma_{bb}(X_{1},X_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Sigma_{bb}(X_{1},X_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In this sense, propagating <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math> through the MLP only requires its diagonal elements and has lower complexity.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Kernel Bounds</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cho and Saul (2009, Theorem 3)</a></cite>, in the infinite width / attention limit <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}^{\mathrm{out}}_{T}\sim\mathcal{GP}(0,\Sigma^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{out}}_{TT})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">out</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}^{\mathrm{out}}_{T}\sim\mathcal{GP}(0,\Sigma^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{out}}_{TT})</annotation></semantics></math>, which results in the GPR predictor</p>
<table id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{T}^{\mathrm{out}}(X_{*})|\{X_{\nu}\}_{\nu=1}^{P},\bm{y}\sim\\
\mathcal{N}(K^{*}\tilde{K}^{-1}\bm{y},k^{*}-K^{*}\tilde{K}^{-1}(K^{*})^{\top})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>out</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{T}^{\mathrm{out}}(X_{*})|\{X_{\nu}\}_{\nu=1}^{P},\bm{y}\sim\\
\mathcal{N}(K^{*}\tilde{K}^{-1}\bm{y},k^{*}-K^{*}\tilde{K}^{-1}(K^{*})^{\top}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">conditioned on the dataset, with symmetric PD <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}=K+\kappa I_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}=K+\kappa I_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), the vector of covariances <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{*}=(K^{*}_{\nu})\equiv(\Sigma^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{out}}_{TT}(X_{*},X_{\nu}))\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">out</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{*}=(K^{*}_{\nu})\equiv(\Sigma^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{out}}_{TT}(X_{*},X_{\nu}))\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}=\Sigma^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{out}}_{TT}(X_{*},X_{*})\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">out</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}=\Sigma^{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{out}}_{TT}(X_{*},X_{*})\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, consider the spectral norm of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is known that</p>
<table id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{K}^{-1}\|_{2}=\\
\sup\left\{\left\lvert\bm{x}_{1}^{\top}\tilde{K}^{-1}\bm{x}_{2}\right\rvert|\bm{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}:\left\lVert\bm{x}_{1}\right\rVert=1=\left\lVert\bm{x}_{2}\right\rVert\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mo>{</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo><mo>}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{K}^{-1}\|_{2}=\\
\sup\left\{\left\lvert\bm{x}_{1}^{\top}\tilde{K}^{-1}\bm{x}_{2}\right\rvert|\bm{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}:\left\lVert\bm{x}_{1}\right\rVert=1=\left\lVert\bm{x}_{2}\right\rVert\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{1}=e_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1}=e_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{2}=e_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{2}=e_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert\tilde{K}^{-1}_{\mu\nu}\right\rvert\leq\left\lVert\tilde{K}^{-1}\right\rVert_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert\tilde{K}^{-1}_{\mu\nu}\right\rvert\leq\left\lVert\tilde{K}^{-1}\right\rVert_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Using the fact that <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric PSD and <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric PD, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Spec\left(\tilde{K}^{-1}\right)=\left\{\frac{1}{\lambda+\kappa}\right|\left.\lambda\in\Spec(K)\vphantom{\frac{1}{\lambda+\kappa}}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Spec</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Spec\left(\tilde{K}^{-1}\right)=\left\{\frac{1}{\lambda+\kappa}\right|\left.\lambda\in\Spec(K)\vphantom{\frac{1}{\lambda+\kappa}}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert\tilde{K}^{-1}_{\mu\nu}\right\rvert\leq\left\lVert\tilde{K}^{-1}\right\rVert_{2}=\max\Spec(\tilde{K}^{-1})\leq\frac{1}{\kappa}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert\tilde{K}^{-1}_{\mu\nu}\right\rvert\leq\left\lVert\tilde{K}^{-1}\right\rVert_{2}=\max\Spec(\tilde{K}^{-1})\leq\frac{1}{\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">As for the <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\times P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\times P</annotation></semantics></math> matrix establishing the RKHS norm in Eq. (<a href="#S5.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ 5.1 Perturbation Theory Estimate ‣ 5 Tighter Bounds and Feature Learning ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), we can play a similar game with</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Spec(\tilde{K}^{-1}K\tilde{K}^{-1})=\left\{\frac{\lambda}{(\lambda+\kappa)^{2}}\right|\left.\lambda\in\Spec(K)\vphantom{\frac{\lambda}{(\lambda+\kappa)^{2}}}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>K</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Spec</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Spec(\tilde{K}^{-1}K\tilde{K}^{-1})=\left\{\frac{\lambda}{(\lambda+\kappa)^{2}}\right|\left.\lambda\in\Spec(K)\vphantom{\frac{\lambda}{(\lambda+\kappa)^{2}}}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\tilde{K}^{-1}K\tilde{K}^{-1}\right\rVert_{2}=\max\Spec(\tilde{K}^{-1}K\tilde{K}^{-1})\leq\frac{1}{4\kappa}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\tilde{K}^{-1}K\tilde{K}^{-1}\right\rVert_{2}=\max\Spec(\tilde{K}^{-1}K\tilde{K}^{-1})\leq\frac{1}{4\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Further Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We trained all models using a standard decoder-only transformer architecture with GeLU activation. We used embedding dimensions of <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=256</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>, number of layer <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=2,4,40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=2,4,40</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=4</annotation></semantics></math> attention heads in each block. For Sorting and Induction, the models utilized Rotary Positional Embeddings (RoPE) to capture relative position information. Training was performed online using the Adam optimizer with a learning rate of <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> and a batch size of <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=512,1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=512,1024</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each task, we followed a two-phase protocol: (1) pre-training, where the model was trained on a fixed input size <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> until it reached a specified accuracy threshold (<math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>), and (2) adaptation, where the pre-trained weights were fine-tuned and evaluated on larger input sizes <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. In all of these experiments, the sample size was computed as the number of epochs times the size of the batch. The sample size (<math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>) reported in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2 Related Work ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> contains only the adaptation cost to larger instances.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For induction we used <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=256,L=2,B=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=256,L=2,B=512</annotation></semantics></math>; for sorting <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=128,L=4,B=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=128,L=4,B=512</annotation></semantics></math>; for shallow SPP we used <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=128,L=4,B=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=128,L=4,B=1024</annotation></semantics></math>; for deep SPP we used <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=128,L=4,B=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=128,L=4,B=1024</annotation></semantics></math>; for shallow MinCut we used <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=128,L=4,B=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=128,L=4,B=1024</annotation></semantics></math>; for deep MinCut we used <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=128,L=40,B=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=128,L=40,B=1024</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Complexity of Score Draws</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The attention kernel estimation involves sampling <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2T^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2T^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> scores, <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ac}(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ac}(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{be}(X_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{be}(X_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which are multivariate Gaussians in the kernel limit. For this purpose, we utilize Kronecker-structured covariance as well as conditioning in multivariate Gaussians to analyze its computational complexity.
First, we consider <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(X_{1})\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(X_{1})\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{vec}(S(X_{1}))\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\Theta(X_{1},X_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{vec}(S(X_{1}))\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\Theta(X_{1},X_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(X_{1},X_{1})=\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(X_{1},X_{1})=\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> as in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 4.3 Kernel Propagation ‣ 4 Low Complexity Bias of Lazy Learning ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). Note that <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> by definition and consequently <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(X_{1},X_{1})\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(X_{1},X_{1})\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a Cholesky decomposition <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})=L_{1}L_{1}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{1},X_{1})=L_{1}L_{1}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can decompose <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(X_{1},X_{1})=(L_{1}\otimes L_{1})(L_{1}\otimes L_{1})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(X_{1},X_{1})=(L_{1}\otimes L_{1})(L_{1}\otimes L_{1})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. An <math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> sample can then be generated at a cost of <math id="A4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(X_{1})=L_{1}UL_{1}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(X_{1})=L_{1}UL_{1}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{ab}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{ab}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we apply Bayes’ rule</p>
<table id="A4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{(S(X_{1}),S(X_{2}))}=p_{S(X_{1})}p_{S(X_{2})\mid S(X_{1})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{(S(X_{1}),S(X_{2}))}=p_{S(X_{1})}p_{S(X_{2})\mid S(X_{1})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The joint covariance of <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S(X_{1}),S(X_{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S(X_{1}),S(X_{2}))</annotation></semantics></math> is the block matrix</p>
<table id="A4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.EGx26.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.EGx26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}\Theta_{11}&amp;\Theta_{12}\\
\Theta_{21}&amp;\Theta_{22}\end{array}\right)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}\Sigma^{\prime}_{11}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{11}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}_{12}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{12}\\
\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}\end{array}\right)\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>22</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>12</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}\Theta_{11}&amp;\Theta_{12}\\
\Theta_{21}&amp;\Theta_{22}\end{array}\right)=\left(\begin{array}[]{cc}\Sigma^{\prime}_{11}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{11}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}_{12}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{12}\\
\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}&amp;\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}\otimes\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}\end{array}\right)\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{ij}\equiv\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{i},X_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{ij}\equiv\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{i},X_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditional distribution of <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(X_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(X_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is known <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">von Mises, 1964</a>, Sec. 9.3)</cite> to be</p>
<table id="A4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S(X_{2})|S(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S(X_{2})|S(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\left(M_{\mathrm{cond}},\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}\left(M_{\mathrm{cond}},\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{\mathrm{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{\mathrm{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Theta_{21}\Theta_{11}^{-1}\mathrm{vec}(S(X_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>11</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>vec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Theta_{21}\Theta_{11}^{-1}\mathrm{vec}(S(X_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Theta_{22}-\Theta_{21}\Theta_{11}^{-1}\Theta_{12}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>11</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Theta_{22}-\Theta_{21}\Theta_{11}^{-1}\Theta_{12}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">which involves calculating</p>
<table id="A4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{\mathrm{cond}}=\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1}S(X_{1})(\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{\mathrm{cond}}=\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1}S(X_{1})(\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.5" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1}\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1}\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math>, again, at a cost of <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          If <math id="footnote7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{11}</annotation></semantics></math> is not positive definite (PD), we can use the Moore-Penrose pseudo-inverse and the conditional becomes degenerate.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To draw a sample from the conditioned Gaussian, we will assume <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{11},\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{11},\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>. We can then calculate</p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H:=L_{2}^{-1}\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1}\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(L_{2}^{\top})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H:=L_{2}^{-1}\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(\Sigma^{\prime}_{11})^{-1}\Sigma^{\prime}_{21}(L_{2}^{\top})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">for a Cholesky decomposition <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}=L_{2}L_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>22</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{22}=L_{2}L_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> at a cost of <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</p>
<table id="A4.p3.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left((L_{2}^{\top})^{-1}\otimes(L_{2})^{-1}\right)\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}\left((L_{2})^{-1}\otimes(L_{2}^{\top})^{-1}\right)=\\
I\otimes I-H\otimes H." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left((L_{2}^{\top})^{-1}\otimes(L_{2})^{-1}\right)\Theta_{\mathrm{cond}}\left((L_{2})^{-1}\otimes(L_{2}^{\top})^{-1}\right)=\\
I\otimes I-H\otimes H.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Since the LHS is PSD, we have <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-H\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-H\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, if we diagonalize <math id="A4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=Q\Lambda Q^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=Q\Lambda Q^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=\mathrm{diag}(\bm{\lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\mathrm{diag}(\bm{\lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}=(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}=(\lambda_{1},\ldots,\lambda_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can generate a sample at a cost of <math id="A4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S(X_{2})|S(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S(X_{2})|S(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=M_{\mathrm{cond}}+L_{2}Q\Delta Q^{\top}L_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=M_{\mathrm{cond}}+L_{2}Q\Delta Q^{\top}L_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sqrt{\bm{1}\bm{1}^{\top}-\bm{\lambda}\bm{\lambda}^{\top}}\odot Q^{-1}U(Q^{\top})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mn>𝟏𝟏</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sqrt{\bm{1}\bm{1}^{\top}-\bm{\lambda}\bm{\lambda}^{\top}}\odot Q^{-1}U(Q^{\top})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{ab}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{ab}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> is matrix element-wise product. To conclude, we obtain a sample of <math id="A4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S(X_{1}),S(X_{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S(X_{1}),S(X_{2}))</annotation></semantics></math> at an overall cost of <math id="A4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Lipschitz Constant of the MLP and Attention Layer Recursions</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Sec. <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Complexity and Accuracy of Kernel Evaluation ‣ 4 Low Complexity Bias of Lazy Learning ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, we established that a single MC estimation of the <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cho and Saul (2009)</a></cite> kernel for the attention layer, using <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{MC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>MC</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{MC}}</annotation></semantics></math> samples, yields an estimation error bounded by <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\sqrt{N_{\mathrm{MC}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>MC</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\sqrt{N_{\mathrm{MC}}})</annotation></semantics></math> irrespective of the sequence length <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. However, evaluating the kernel of a deep transformer involves a sequential chain of estimations, where the empirically evaluated covariance matrix from layer <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is passed into the non-linear Gaussian expectations of layer <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
A critical theoretical concern is whether the accumulation of MC errors across layers magnifies extensively with the sequence length <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. If the error magnification were to scale as <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, maintaining a constant target accuracy at the network’s output would require the number of MC samples <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{MC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>MC</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{MC}}</annotation></semantics></math> to grow polynomially or above with <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby invalidating our inference complexity bounds.
Here we show that this does not occur. We show that the layer-to-layer kernel recursion maps for both the attention and MLP layers are Lipschitz continuous with respect to the matrix max-norm, and, crucially, that their Lipschitz constants are strictly <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and independent of <math id="A5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will let <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the true pre-activation covariance matrix at a given layer, while <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}+\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}+\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>
will be its MC estimate, with a max-norm estimation error of <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}=\max_{a,b}\left\lvert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}_{ab}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}=\max_{a,b}\left\lvert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}_{ab}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>. Because standard transformer architectures employ LayerNorm, the pre-activation covariance elements are strictly bounded by a constant, which we denote by <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq M=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq M=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Error Propagation in the Attention Layer</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us pick a pair of tokens <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math> and of inputs <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{1}:=S_{a\bullet}^{h=1}(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{1}:=S_{a\bullet}^{h=1}(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{s}_{2}:=S_{b\bullet}^{h=1}(X_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∙</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{2}:=S_{b\bullet}^{h=1}(X_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, both considered random vectors in <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            Taking the expectation over <math id="footnote8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1,\ldots,H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1,\ldots,H</annotation></semantics></math> implies that we may choose a single head to evaluate for, here, chosen arbitrarily to be <math id="footnote8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> By Eq. (<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 4.3 Kernel Propagation ‣ 4 Low Complexity Bias of Lazy Learning ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), the exact attention kernel recursion is given by</p>
<table id="A5.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})}\left[f(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}(X_{1},X_{2})A_{e}(\bm{s}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}(X_{1},X_{2})A_{e}(\bm{s}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\bm{s}_{i})_{c}=\Softmax\left(\bm{s}_{i}\right)_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\bm{s}_{i})_{c}=\Softmax\left(\bm{s}_{i}\right)_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2T</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional random vector <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{s}}:=(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{s}}:=(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> follows a multivariate Gaussian distribution <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,C)</annotation></semantics></math> with covariance matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}^{2T\times 2T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}^{2T\times 2T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A perturbation introduced in the previous layer affects the attention layer output in two ways: it shifts <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}\to\Sigma^{\prime}+\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}\to\Sigma^{\prime}+\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to C+\Delta C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to C+\Delta C</annotation></semantics></math>. We can then bound the total discrepancy <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> using the triangle inequality</p>
<table id="A5.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert\Delta\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2})\right\rvert\leq e_{\mathrm{val}}+e_{\mathrm{measure}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert\Delta\Sigma_{ab}(X_{1},X_{2})\right\rvert\leq e_{\mathrm{val}}+e_{\mathrm{measure}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the first contribution comes from the direct effect on <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and the second from the indirect effect via <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1. Bounding <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\mathrm{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\mathrm{val}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The error induced by substituting <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}\to\Sigma^{\prime}+\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}\to\Sigma^{\prime}+\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A5.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e_{\mathrm{val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e_{\mathrm{val}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\lvert\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{s}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,C+\Delta C)}\left[\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}A_{e}(\bm{s}_{2})\right]\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\lvert\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{s}}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,C+\Delta C)}\left[\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}A_{e}(\bm{s}_{2})\right]\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\mathbb{E}_{(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})}\left[\left(\sum_{c=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})\right)\left(\sum_{e=1}^{T}A_{e}(\bm{s}_{2})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\mathbb{E}_{(\bm{s}_{1},\bm{s}_{2})}\left[\left(\sum_{c=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{s}_{1})\right)\left(\sum_{e=1}^{T}A_{e}(\bm{s}_{2})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The 2nd inequality results from <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Softmax" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Softmax</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Softmax</annotation></semantics></math> outputs summing up to <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. The valuation error, thus, perfectly absorbs the <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> summands and is exactly <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz and independent of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2. Bounding <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{\mathrm{measure}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{\mathrm{measure}}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we evaluate the shift in the expectation due to the perturbed distribution of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As established in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 4.3 Kernel Propagation ‣ 4 Low Complexity Bias of Lazy Learning ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), the covariance <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> factorizes as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{(i,c),(j,e)}=(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{(i,c),(j,e)}=(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{ij}\equiv\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{i},X_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{ij}\equiv\Sigma^{\prime}(X_{i},X_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. Under perturbation, the corresponding score covariance block is shifted</p>
<table id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\to\\
\left((\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}+(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}\right)\left((\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}+(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\to\\
\left((\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}+(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}\right)\left((\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}+(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The difference in the score covariance matrices is then</p>
<table id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}=(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}+\\
(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}+(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}=(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}+\\
(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}+(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ab}(\Delta\Sigma_{ij}^{\prime})_{ce}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq 2M\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}+\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq 2M\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}+\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To bound the shift in expectation under the perturbed Gaussian measure, we employ a multivariate Gaussian interpolation technique – a standard application of Gaussian integration by parts, often associated with Price’s Theorem. We construct a continuous interpolation between the unperturbed covariance <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and the perturbed covariance <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C+\Delta C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C+\Delta C</annotation></semantics></math> parameterized by <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(t):=C+t\Delta C." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(t):=C+t\Delta C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\tilde{\bm{S}}(t))=\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{S}^{(1)}(t)A_{e}(\bm{S}^{(2)}(t))\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\tilde{\bm{S}}(t))=\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{S}^{(1)}(t)A_{e}(\bm{S}^{(2)}(t))\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)=(\bm{S}^{(1)}(t),\bm{S}^{(2)}(t))\sim\mathcal{N}(0,C(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)=(\bm{S}^{(1)}(t),\bm{S}^{(2)}(t))\sim\mathcal{N}(0,C(t))</annotation></semantics></math> be a Gaussian random vector defined along this path, and let us define the expected value of our function as a parameterized scalar function of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi(t)=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[f(\tilde{\bm{S}})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi(t)=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[f(\tilde{\bm{S}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The total error introduced by the measure pathway is the absolute difference at the endpoints, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}=\left\lvert\varphi(1)-\varphi(0)\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}=\left\lvert\varphi(1)-\varphi(0)\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>. By the fundamental theorem of calculus, this is bounded by the absolute integral of its derivative:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}=\left\lvert\int_{0}^{1}\varphi^{\prime}(t)dt\right\rvert\leq\int_{0}^{1}\left\lvert\varphi^{\prime}(t)\right\rvert dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}=\left\lvert\int_{0}^{1}\varphi^{\prime}(t)dt\right\rvert\leq\int_{0}^{1}\left\lvert\varphi^{\prime}(t)\right\rvert dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">To compute <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we utilize Price’s Theorem, which establishes that for a twice-differentiable function <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, the derivative of its Gaussian expectation with respect to the covariance elements is exactly half the expectation of its corresponding second spatial derivatives. Applying the multivariate chain rule yields:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\frac{dC_{(i,c),(j,e)}(t)}{dt}\frac{\partial}{\partial C_{(i,c),(j,e)}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[f(\tilde{\bm{S}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\frac{dC_{(i,c),(j,e)}(t)}{dt}\frac{\partial}{\partial C_{(i,c),(j,e)}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[f(\tilde{\bm{S}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Substituting this back into the integral, we can apply the triangle inequality to bring the absolute value inside the expectation. We then bound each covariance perturbation by the matrix max-norm, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\right\rvert\leq\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\right\rvert\leq\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, and pull this constant outside the summation:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{i,j,c,e}\left\lvert\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\right\rvert\,\left\lvert\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right]\right\rvert dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{i,j,c,e}\left\lvert\Delta C_{(i,c),(j,e)}\right\rvert\,\left\lvert\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right]\right\rvert dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[\sum_{i,j,c,e}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right\rvert\right]dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\bm{S}}(t)}\left[\sum_{i,j,c,e}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right\rvert\right]dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Finally, we can obtain a strict, distribution-free upper bound by replacing the integrand with its supremum over all possible spatial realizations <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{S}}\in\mathbb{R}^{2T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{S}}\in\mathbb{R}^{2T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because this supremum is strictly independent of the interpolation parameter <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the integral trivially evaluates to 1, leaving us with the bound:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}\leq\frac{1}{2}\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}\sup_{\tilde{\bm{S}}}\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right\rvert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}\leq\frac{1}{2}\left\lVert\Delta C\right\rVert_{\infty}\sup_{\tilde{\bm{S}}}\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f(\tilde{\bm{S}})}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we bound the <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm (the sum of absolute values) by showing each summand scales as <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/T^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/T^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. To this end, we use the algebraic constraints set on the <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{c}({\bm{s}}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{c}({\bm{s}}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> by the Softmax.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Absolute Hessian Sum of Softmax)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{c}=\Softmax(\bm{S})_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{c}=\Softmax(\bm{S})_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sum of the absolute values of its first and second derivatives with respect to the logits <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}</annotation></semantics></math> are universally bounded independently of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial A_{c}}{\partial S_{k}}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial A_{c}}{\partial S_{k}}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2A_{c}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2A_{c},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}A_{c}}{\partial S_{k}\partial S_{l}}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}A_{c}}{\partial S_{k}\partial S_{l}}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 6A_{c}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 6A_{c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first derivatives are <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{k}A_{c}=A_{c}(\delta_{ck}-A_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{k}A_{c}=A_{c}(\delta_{ck}-A_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking the absolute sum:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{T}\left\lvert A_{c}(\delta_{ck}-A_{k})\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{T}\left\lvert A_{c}(\delta_{ck}-A_{k})\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A_{c}(1-A_{c})+\sum_{k\neq c}A_{c}A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A_{c}(1-A_{c})+\sum_{k\neq c}A_{c}A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2A_{c}(1-A_{c})\leq 2A_{c}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2A_{c}(1-A_{c})\leq 2A_{c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The second derivatives are derived via the product rule:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial^{2}_{kl}A_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial^{2}_{kl}A_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{l}}\left(A_{c}\delta_{ck}-A_{c}A_{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial}{\partial S_{l}}\left(A_{c}\delta_{ck}-A_{c}A_{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A_{c}\delta_{ck}\delta_{cl}-A_{c}A_{l}\delta_{ck}-A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{cl}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A_{c}\delta_{ck}\delta_{cl}-A_{c}A_{l}\delta_{ck}-A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{cl}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{kl}+2A_{c}A_{k}A_{l}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{kl}+2A_{c}A_{k}A_{l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the triangle inequality and summing over <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,l</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\partial^{2}_{kl}A_{c}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\partial^{2}_{kl}A_{c}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\Big(A_{c}\delta_{ck}\delta_{cl}+A_{c}A_{l}\delta_{ck}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\Big(A_{c}\delta_{ck}\delta_{cl}+A_{c}A_{l}\delta_{ck}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad+A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{cl}+A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{kl}+2A_{c}A_{k}A_{l}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad+A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{cl}+A_{c}A_{k}\delta_{kl}+2A_{c}A_{k}A_{l}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{T}A_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{T}A_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the summations directly evaluate to:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\partial^{2}_{kl}A_{c}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\partial^{2}_{kl}A_{c}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq A_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq A_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+A_{c}(1)+A_{c}(1)+A_{c}(1)+2A_{c}(1)=6A_{c}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+A_{c}(1)+A_{c}(1)+A_{c}(1)+2A_{c}(1)=6A_{c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We apply Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma E.1 (Absolute Hessian Sum of Softmax). ‣ 2. Bounding 𝑒_measure ‣ E.1 Error Propagation in the Attention Layer ‣ Appendix E Lipschitz Constant of the MLP and Attention Layer Recursions ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> to our integrand <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\tilde{\bm{S}})=\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{S}^{(1)})A_{e}(\bm{S}^{(2)})\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}(X_{1},X_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\tilde{\bm{S}})=\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}A_{c}(\bm{S}^{(1)})A_{e}(\bm{S}^{(2)})\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}(X_{1},X_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, and adopt a shorthand notation <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{c}({\bm{S}}^{(1)}))=A_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{c}({\bm{S}}^{(1)}))=A_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{e}({\bm{S}}^{(2)}))=A_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{e}({\bm{S}}^{(2)}))=A_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the product rule, the absolute Hessian over all <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2T\times 2T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2T\times 2T</annotation></semantics></math> variables decomposes into three blocks:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i,j,k,l=1}^{2,2,T,T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i,j,k,l=1}^{2,2,T,T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,k)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,l)}}\right\rvert=\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}\partial S^{(1)}_{l}}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,k)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,l)}}\right\rvert=\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}\partial S^{(1)}_{l}}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial S^{(2)}_{k}\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right\rvert+2\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right\rvert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial S^{(2)}_{k}\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right\rvert+2\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">We bound each block sequentially. For the first block:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}\left(\frac{\partial^{2}A_{c}}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}\partial S^{(1)}_{l}}\right)A_{e}\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}\left(\frac{\partial^{2}A_{c}}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}\partial S^{(1)}_{l}}\right)A_{e}\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}(6A_{c})A_{e}\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}(6A_{c})A_{e}\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 6\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq 6M." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 6\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq 6M.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">By symmetry, the second block is also bounded by <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6M</annotation></semantics></math>. For the cross-derivative block:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k,l=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lvert\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}\left(\frac{\partial A_{c}}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}}\right)\left(\frac{\partial A_{e}}{\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right)\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lvert\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}\left(\frac{\partial A_{c}}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}}\right)\left(\frac{\partial A_{e}}{\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right)\Sigma^{\prime}_{ce}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}\left(\sum_{k=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial A_{c}}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}}\right\rvert\right)\left(\sum_{l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial A_{e}}{\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right\rvert\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\lVert\Sigma^{\prime}\right\rVert_{\infty}\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}\left(\sum_{k=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial A_{c}}{\partial S^{(1)}_{k}}\right\rvert\right)\left(\sum_{l=1}^{T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial A_{e}}{\partial S^{(2)}_{l}}\right\rvert\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq M\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}(2A_{c})(2A_{e})=4M." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq M\sum_{c,e=1}^{T}(2A_{c})(2A_{e})=4M.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Substituting these into Eq. (<a href="#A5.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ 2. Bounding 𝑒_measure ‣ E.1 Error Propagation in the Attention Layer ‣ Appendix E Lipschitz Constant of the MLP and Attention Layer Recursions ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), the absolute Hessian sum of the entire <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2T</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional integrand is universally bounded:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\tilde{\bm{S}}}\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑺</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\tilde{\bm{S}}}\sum_{i,j,c,e=1}^{2,2,T,T}\left\lvert\frac{\partial^{2}f}{\partial\tilde{S}_{(i,c)}\partial\tilde{S}_{(j,e)}}\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 6M+6M+2(4M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 6M+6M+2(4M)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=20M." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=20M.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Applying this to Eq. (<a href="#A5.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ 2. Bounding 𝑒_measure ‣ E.1 Error Propagation in the Attention Layer ‣ Appendix E Lipschitz Constant of the MLP and Attention Layer Recursions ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), the error along the Gaussian measure pathway is bounded by:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}\leq\frac{1}{2}(2M\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}+\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}^{2})(20M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}\leq\frac{1}{2}(2M\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}+\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}^{2})(20M)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=20M^{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}+10M\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=20M^{2}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}+10M\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the value and measure error, and taking the leading order term for reasonably bounded estimation errors (assuming <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>), the maximum propagation error through the attention layer is strictly bounded by:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\mathrm{next}}\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>next</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\mathrm{next}}\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{val}}+\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>measure</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{val}}+\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{measure}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1+30M^{2})\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1+30M^{2})\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">The Lipschitz constant of the attention kernel recursion is <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{attn}}=1+30M^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>attn</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{attn}}=1+30M^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, this constant is independent of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Error Propagation in the MLP Layer</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As outlined in App. <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Kernel Propagation ‣ Appendix A Transformers in Detail ‣ Algorithmic Capture, Computational Complexity, and Inductive Bias of Infinite Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, the propagation through an MLP layer relies strictly on the diagonal elements of the token-to-token matrix. The update rule is element-wise:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma^{\mathrm{next}}_{ab}=\sigma_{\bm{b}}^{2}+\sigma_{W}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{(z_{a},z_{b})\sim\mathcal{N}(0,k)}\left[\phi(z_{a})\phi(z_{b})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>next</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝒃</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma^{\mathrm{next}}_{ab}=\sigma_{\bm{b}}^{2}+\sigma_{W}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{(z_{a},z_{b})\sim\mathcal{N}(0,k)}\left[\phi(z_{a})\phi(z_{b})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, the Gaussian expectation operates over a bivariate normal distribution parameterized entirely by the <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> covariance matrix <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, whose elements are comprised of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{aa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{aa}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}_{bb}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}_{bb}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because there is no summation or mixing across the <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> sequence indices, a perturbation <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> in the input covariance matrix merely perturbs the <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> matrix <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> by at most <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For standard activation functions bounded by linear growth (e.g., ReLU or GeLU), the dual activation integral is known to be smooth and uniformly Lipschitz continuous with respect to the input covariance entries <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schoenholz et al., 2017</a>)</cite>. Consequently, the local error simply scales by a bounded, architecture-dependent constant <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{mlp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>mlp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{mlp}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\mathrm{next}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{mlp}}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>next</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>mlp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\Delta\Sigma^{\mathrm{next}}\right\rVert_{\infty}\leq\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{mlp}}\left\lVert\Delta\right\rVert_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. This integration acts strictly locally in the sequence dimension and inherently exhibits zero dependence on <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Conclusion</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since both the Attention and MLP kernel recursions possess <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-independent max-norm Lipschitz bounds, an initial Monte Carlo error <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> at the first layer will magnify to at most <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{L}\leq(\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{attn}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{mlp}})^{L}\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>attn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>mlp</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{L}\leq(\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{attn}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{mlp}})^{L}\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> after <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers. For a finite-depth network, this is a fixed constant scaling factor.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consequently, to ensure that the final estimated kernel maintains an absolute approximation error <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lvert f^{\mathrm{MC}}_{\delta}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\rvert&lt;\Delta/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi><mi>MC</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lvert f^{\mathrm{MC}}_{\delta}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\rvert&lt;\Delta/6</annotation></semantics></math>, the required estimation precision per layer does not depend on the context length <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. The necessary number of Monte Carlo samples <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{MC}}\propto 1/\epsilon_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>MC</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{MC}}\propto 1/\epsilon_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> therefore remains agnostic of <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
